  "music": "w2-sizzle-street",
  "authorNotes": "Solo, no chain required. This is the belt taught alone: grab camera-1 near spawn, then step onto belt-tutorial (650,900 to 1350,900, speed 90) — a safety plank (600,1150 to 1350,1210) runs the whole length directly beneath it, so riding the belt is the level's first ~15s and carries zero death risk even on a bad landing, matching the '20s' rule with margin. The belt drops you flush onto the mid counter at 1350. The only real risk in the level is the second crossing: swing-crossing (pivot 1650,620, 260px reach) over the true void to the goal counter at 2150 — the first genuine fall in Sizzle Street, arriving well past the safe window. Snap the photo (allAirborne) mid-arc on that swing. An assist beam spans the same gap for players who'd rather not trust the last grab. No heat, no grease, no relics yet — this level is the conveyor and nothing else."
